@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.user.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Contact Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account contact information transfers properly to the account index.

Setup:
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | usr.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | USR                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | usr.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | USR                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | usr.koroneiki3                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | USR                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki3                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | usr.koroneiki4                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | USR                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki4                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | usr.koroneiki5                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki5@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | USR                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki5                           |
	| Email Status  | UNVERIFIED                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Oneusr - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| User Site Partner |
	| Changed Partner   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki5@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki5@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki5@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki5@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay User Customer Role |
	| Second User Customer Role  |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korusr - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oneusr - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| USRKORKORUSR |
	| ONEUSRONEUSR |
	| USRKOR       |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Korusr - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| USRKORKORUSR |
	| ONEUSRONEUSR |
	| USRKOR       |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki5@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Korusr - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oneusr - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View contact
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the ability to create a contact in Dossiera and viewing the respective contact in the provisioning account details page

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | USR                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | USR                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki4                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Korusr - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I create a team with the name "User Site Partner" for the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "User Site Partner" on the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "User Site Partner"
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "nHZMPLWyzvRKujPLqfHK"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korusr"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Contacts" tab
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | USR Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Support Watcher                      |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                             |
	When I click on the "Liferay Workers" tab
	Then I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Auto > Assigned Contact" and "USR Koroneiki1" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Assigned Contact > USR Koroneiki1 |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                      |
	| Update Field New Value      | Support Watcher                          |

Scenario: View contact added via New Project Existing Business message
	Testing the ability to create a contact via an Existing Business message in Dossiera and viewing the respective contact in the provisioning account details page

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | USRKOR                        | |
	| Name   | Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	And I create an external link for the account "Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And I create an external link for the account "Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | USR                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | USR                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki4                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Korusr - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Project Existing Business              |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I create a team with the name "User Site Partner" for the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "User Site Partner" on the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "User Site Partner"
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "nHZMPLWyzvRKujPLqfHK"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korusr"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Contacts" tab
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | USR Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Support Watcher                      |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                             |
	When I click on the "Liferay Workers" tab
	Then I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

